# Coleccion para la extension REST Client de VS Code.
# Define adminPassword y token en la configuracion privada de VS Code o en una copia local ignorada.
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8080
@adminEmail = admin@example.com
@adminPassword = REEMPLAZAR_LOCALMENTE
@token = PEGAR_JWT_LOCALMENTE
@userId = 11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111
@userEmail = prueba-local@example.test
@userPassword = CambiarEstaClave123!

### Verificar OpenAPI
GET {{baseUrl}}/v3/api-docs

### Crear usuario publico: solo MEMBER; debe responder 201/PENDING
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "{{userId}}",
  "name": "Prueba Local",
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "password": "{{userPassword}}",
  "role": "MEMBER"
}

### Login de usuario PENDING: debe responder 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "password": "{{userPassword}}"
}

### Login administrador local: copiar accessToken en token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### Listar: 200 con ADMIN o REVIEWER; 401 sin JWT
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Obtener por ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Activar usuario: requiere ADMIN
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Prueba Local Activa",
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "password": "",
  "role": "MEMBER",
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### Login de usuario ACTIVE: debe responder 200 con JWT
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "password": "{{userPassword}}"
}

### Eliminar: requiere ADMIN, responde 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
